MID_SE_Die_Hal_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_001: Hup, hup, hup! Not bad! Not bad at all! But...am I\nbeing watched?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_002: I don't see anyone, but it feels like someone is staring\nat me. Could it be...a ghost or something?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_003: I'm surprised you noticed me. I'm usually pretty good\nat blending into the foliage.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_004: Aaah! Diego?! I-I'm the surprised one!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_005: Why's that? I thought you'd already noticed me\nperched up in the tree.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_006: Not really... It just felt like someone was staring...\nKinda like when I have an engaged audience.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_007: Huh. Spoken like a true professional.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_008: I don't know about all that...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_009: So you were watching me practice, huh?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_010: Yeah. I was impressed too. You have a lot of daggers\nin the air, but you never lose control.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_011: But I wasn't watching to pass the time. I wanted to\nstudy your form.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_012: I thought Orchel might like to see me juggle.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_013: I don't really know what you mean, but it seems like\nyou wanna learn.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_014: Well then, want to give it a go? I'm happy to\nteach you.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_015: No kidding? Let's get started.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_016: OK! We'll begin with just one dagger. Pay attention\nto your center of gravity.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_017: Got it. Hm, this dagger seems light...is it fake?\nWell, doesn't matter.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_018: Hah. Hup. Hraugh... I keep losing it as soon as I go\nup to three.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_019: But you're really getting it! You're learning\nso quickly!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_020: For Orchel's sake, I can't learn quickly enough.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_021: Well then, why don't you borrow my daggers? And if\nyou come find me again, I'll keep teaching you.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_022: I appreciate that. Out of curiosity...do you ever use\nreal daggers in the act?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_023: Of course not. That'd be way too dangerous. Why do\nyou ask?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_024: It just occurred to me that it could be a good way to\ncatch someone off guard.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_C_025: Do you mean so I could kill them or something?!\nAgh, you really are kinda scary!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_001: Hup, hup, hup! That's enough practice for now.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_002: Wow, amazing! You are so skilled!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_003: Am I? It's hard for me to judge.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_004: Absolutely. I mean, it wasn't until recently that I\nstarted to get any good at it.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_005: You improved so quickly. Maybe you don't even need\nmy help anymore...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_006: Are you kidding? I wouldn't have gotten this far\nwithout you. Thanks.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_007: No way, it can't be because of me... Or could it?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_008: Though I did add my own spin on what you showed\nme. Want to see?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_009: Ooo, you did?! Show me, show me!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_010: Hah... Hm... Hup...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_011: Whoa! The dagger is so high, I can't even see it...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_012: Halvin.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_013: Huh? Where'd he go?
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_014: Wait, where's the dagger? My...stomach...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_015: Yah! Did the dagger get me?!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_016: Maybe I'm not useful anymore, now that you know\nall I can teach you! Please, spare meee!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_017: Why are you freaking out? Open your eyes so I can\nshow you what I came up with.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_018: Wait...no dagger? It's...a bunch of flowers?!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_019: I wanted to thank you for all your help. But I got\nnervous and bumped you.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_020: Oh, oh, ohhhh. I see! That's all it was. You really\nthrew me for a loop.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_021: Diverting the person's attention and using that\nmoment to grab something—super practical!
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_022: Yeah, you can pick up whatever weapon you need.\nAnd as you've seen, it's good for closing the distance.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_023: A weapon? So you do plan to use this trick for\nsomething risky...
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_024: There's no risk involved if I practice enough to\nensure the kill.
MID_SE_Die_Hal_B_025: That's not what it means to knock an audience dead!